answer.en:
Use an async generator on the server and a browser-readable stream on the client. FastAPI's **StreamingResponse** sends each yielded chunk; SSE adds event framing, while `fetch` can consume `Response.body` chunk by chunk. Define chunk boundaries and cancellation explicitly.

```python caption="A generator yields model text as it arrives; cancellation must reach the upstream client."
from collections.abc import AsyncIterable
from fastapi import FastAPI
from fastapi.responses import StreamingResponse

app = FastAPI()

async def model_tokens() -> AsyncIterable[str]:
    async for token in provider.stream():
        yield token

@app.post("/chat")
async def chat():
    return StreamingResponse(model_tokens(), media_type="text/plain")
```

```ts caption="Read each UTF-8 chunk and stop the request when the user cancels."
const controller = new AbortController();
const response = await fetch("/chat", { method: "POST", body: JSON.stringify({ prompt }), signal: controller.signal });
const reader = response.body!.pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream()).getReader();
for (;;) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  renderToken(value);
}
```

Do not assume one network chunk equals one token. Test disconnects, upstream errors, partial output, proxy buffering, and cancellation.

answer.es:
Usá un generador asíncrono en el servidor y un stream legible por el navegador en el cliente. **StreamingResponse** de FastAPI envía cada chunk producido; SSE agrega framing de eventos, mientras que `fetch` puede consumir `Response.body` de a partes. Definí los límites de cada chunk y la cancelación explícitamente.

```python caption="Un generador entrega el texto del modelo a medida que llega; la cancelación debe alcanzar al cliente upstream."
from collections.abc import AsyncIterable
from fastapi import FastAPI
from fastapi.responses import StreamingResponse

app = FastAPI()

async def model_tokens() -> AsyncIterable[str]:
    async for token in provider.stream():
        yield token

@app.post("/chat")
async def chat():
    return StreamingResponse(model_tokens(), media_type="text/plain")
```

```ts caption="Leé cada chunk UTF-8 y frená el request cuando la persona cancela."
const controller = new AbortController();
const response = await fetch("/chat", { method: "POST", body: JSON.stringify({ prompt }), signal: controller.signal });
const reader = response.body!.pipeThrough(new TextDecoderStream()).getReader();
for (;;) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read();
  if (done) break;
  renderToken(value);
}
```

No supongas que un chunk de red equivale a un token. Probá cortes, errores del upstream, salida parcial, buffering del proxy y cancelación.
